{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23441 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is implicated in the interaction with LAMA-84 through a series of molecular targets, primarily through the dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is targeted by multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, CID 21778290, and Astersaponin F, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of LAMA-84. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Corticatic Acid E may act as a modulator or activator of these kinases, which in turn influence LAMA-84. The integration of these targets highlights a possible mechanism involving kinase activation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same kinase implies a broader role for Corticatic Acid E in regulating LAMA-84, potentially through a shared downstream effect.",
